    {
      "text": "Single-phase fcc FeCoNi or a close derivative has high saturation magnetization and coercivity at or below approximately 100 Oe.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 1–3 at.% Nb during alloy processing will promote formation of nanoscale precipitates in the fcc matrix.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting nanoscale precipitates will be Nb-rich.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-rich precipitates will be dispersed within an fcc FeCoNi-based matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb-rich precipitates act as pinning centers for magnetic domain walls during magnetization reversal.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Domain-wall pinning by the precipitates creates additional energy barriers to domain-wall motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The additional barriers to domain-wall motion will increase the coercive field.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-modified alloy should have a coercive field greater than approximately 100 Oe.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The increase in coercivity will be accompanied by at most a modest decrease in saturation magnetization.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Suitable synthesis and heat treatment can favor heterogeneous nucleation of Nb-rich precipitates without substantially changing the FeCoNi-based matrix composition.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coercivity response depends on precipitate size, distribution, and volume fraction.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive precipitate size or a substantial change in overall phase constitution may prevent the proposed coercivity improvement.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Poorly controlled Nb addition may adversely affect saturation magnetization.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
